From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Run the storage service in the browser process on Windows

Return no sandboxed storage directory on Windows, so the storage service
runs in the browser process (the path --single-process takes) instead of
a utility process. One process, its threads and its JIT pool copies
fewer under Playport (PLA-384).
Apply after the pinned CEF stock patches.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-17-cef-trim.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
index caccaf08e6..86127f98ec 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -7236,10 +7236,16 @@ void ChromeContentBrowserClient::OnNetworkServiceDataUseUpdate(
 
 base::FilePath
 ChromeContentBrowserClient::GetSandboxedStorageServiceDataDirectory() {
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+  // No directory on Windows: the storage service runs in the browser process,
+  // for an embedder that must fit several processes in a small address space.
+  return base::FilePath();
+#else
   if (!g_browser_process || !g_browser_process->profile_manager()) {
     return base::FilePath();
   }
   return g_browser_process->profile_manager()->user_data_dir();
+#endif
 }
 
 bool ChromeContentBrowserClient::ShouldSandboxAudioService() {
